<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Qualcomm CAF trees for the SDM670, pinned at their newest upstream revision.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
  LineageOS removed CAF support for sdm845 (and msm8996/msm8998) in
  android @ a462d457ca85 "manifest: Remove legacy repositories" (2026-06-21).
  That commit deleted the three project entries AND the linkfile that creates
  the hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845 soong namespace. The removal happened while the
  branches were still at their 23.2 revisions, so there is no 24.0 work to
  move to: lineage-23.2-caf-sdm845 is the newest branch that exists upstream
  for android_hardware_qcom_audio, android_hardware_qcom_display and
  android_hardware_qcom_media. Verified against the 23.2 tree, whose checkouts
  of these three repos sit at exactly these SHAs.

  WHY IT BLOCKS THE BUILD
  vendor/samsung/gts4lv-common/Android.bp:5 (generated by our own
  device/samsung/gts4lv-common/extract-files.py:22) declares a soong_namespace
  importing "hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845". With the namespace absent, Soong aborts
  before ninja runs:

    error: vendor/samsung/gts4lv-common/Android.bp:5:1: module "soong_namespace":
    namespace hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845 does not exist

  That namespace is not cosmetic. 22 modules are referenced from it by the
  vendor blobs and by our device tree, 7 of them hard shared_libs link
  dependencies (mm-pp-dpps -> libqdutils, and others). None of the 22 resolve
  from any other namespace present in the 24.0 tree, so deleting the import
  would only move the failure into the link step.

  Same pattern as L5: repos with no official lineage-24.0 branch keep their
  older revision (device/samsung/gts4lv, gts4lvwifi and the TheMuppets vendor
  repos are all still on lineage-22.2 for the same reason).

  RISK
  These are 23.2 CAF trees in a 24.0 platform. 23.2 is the combination that is
  known to build; 23.2 CAF against 24.0 platform is not. If it compiles the
  likely friction is in audio/display/media HAL surface, VINTF, and HIDL
  binder. This file is self-contained and reversible: delete it and re-sync.
-->
<manifest>
  <!-- No <remote> here on purpose. The "github" remote is defined in
       LineageOS/android default.xml and redeclaring it here without a fetch
       attribute replaces it with a remote that has no URL, which makes
       repo sync fail with "no fetch in <remote>". Inheriting is correct. -->

  <!-- SDM670 CAF. Pinned to the newest revision that exists upstream; there is
       no lineage-24.0-caf-sdm845 branch in any of these three repos. -->
  <project path="hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845/audio"
           name="LineageOS/android_hardware_qcom_audio"
           remote="github" revision="lineage-23.2-caf-sdm845" />

  <project path="hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845/display"
           name="LineageOS/android_hardware_qcom_display"
           remote="github" revision="lineage-23.2-caf-sdm845" />

  <project path="hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845/media"
           name="LineageOS/android_hardware_qcom_media"
           remote="github" revision="lineage-23.2-caf-sdm845" />

  <!-- Recreates hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845/Android.bp, which upstream a462d457ca85
       removed along with the three projects. That file is what declares the
       hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845 soong_namespace the vendor blobs import; without
       it the modules synced above would sit in no namespace at all.

       extend-project, not project: the linkfile must be declared inside the
       hardware/qcom-caf/common project because src is resolved relative to that
       project's path, and repo only accepts <linkfile> as a child of a project
       node. extend-project merges into the existing project, so upstream's own
       linkfiles for msm8953/sdm660/sm8150/... are kept rather than restated
       here and going stale. -->
  <extend-project name="LineageOS/android_hardware_qcom-caf_common"
                  path="hardware/qcom-caf/common" remote="github">
    <linkfile src="os_pickup_qssi.bp" dest="hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845/Android.bp" />
  </extend-project>
</manifest>